From ff4f44df57404262bc10a68a732af44bf60788a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronghua Zeng <ronghuaz@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] qapp: reduce flash and RAM for WPA3-Enterprise on QCC730
 fullmac

QCC730 is a fullmac device: Wi-Fi firmware handles all scan, connect,
and disconnect operations internally, leaving the host supplicant to
run only the EAP authentication state machine.  This commit trims the
build to reflect this, saving ~120 KB flash and ~22 KB RAM.

ent_app/prj.conf changes:

P0-1  CONFIG_WIFI_NM_WPA_SUPPLICANT_NO_DEBUG=y
  Remove wpa_printf format strings from rodata (~50-70 KB flash).

P0-2  CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C=n
  QCC730 is a Wi-Fi client; TLS server-side code (ssl_tls12_server.c,
  ssl_tls13_server.c) is unreachable at runtime (~4 KB flash).

P1-1  CONFIG_WIFI_NM_WPA_SUPPLICANT_THREAD_STACK_SIZE=65536
  Reduce supplicant thread stack from 80 KB to 64 KB (-16 KB RAM).
  EAP-TLS (deepest stack path) passes regression at 64 KB.

P2    CONFIG_WIFI_NM_WPA_SUPPLICANT_FULLMAC=y
  Exclude scan.c, sme.c, bss.c, ctrl_iface.c, ctrl_iface_zephyr.c,
  wpa_cli_cmds.c, wpa_cli_zephyr.c from the build (~101 KB flash).

P3-3  CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_ALL_ENABLED=n + CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256R1_ENABLED=y
  Restrict ECP curves to secp256r1 (P-256); enterprise test cases use
  only AKM5/WPA2-Enterprise, none require Suite B 192-bit (P-384).
